{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/517264-blood-dimmed-tides-merfolk-and-playing-beneath-the-waves","id":517264,"title":"Blood Dimmed Tides, Merfolk and playing beneath the waves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-17T12:55:33-07:00","id":517264,"title":"Blood Dimmed Tides, Merfolk and playing beneath the waves","content":"I recently read Blood Dimmed Tides, and really liked some parts of it, especially the merfolk chapter. Has someone on the forum played an underwater changeling campaign using the book, or a story with merfloks on the surface? <br /> Also, has someone run into trouble with House Melusine? I'm mostly bothered by the fact that they live in underwater cities when they can't even spend a good night's sleep there without being fed mermaid milk. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T21:28:19-07:00","id":517628,"title":"","content":"I dream of playing an Aquatic Gangrel someday. <br /> <br /> The Wraith content is surprisingly usable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T07:12:41-07:00","id":517956,"title":"","content":"I never played Wraith, but I did like the fluff about them. Pirates, vengeful ex-slaves, haunted seas... the oceans of the dead sure are busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:56:26-07:00","id":518260,"title":"","content":"The problem with playing 'beneath the waves' (and I think this point is actually brought up in the book) is that there is a <b><i>lot</i></b> of space down there, and not a lot that we players, being land-dwellers, would recognize as compelling story material.<br /> <br /> That said, this is the World of Darkness, so playing fast and loose with 'reality' is kind of a given. The Gauntlet/Shroud is basically <i>nil</i>, except perhaps around Mage enclaves and Cousteau-style ocean explorers, so feel free to throw in spirits, spectres, chimera, and what-all-else coming and going as they please, to say nothing of other established supernatural populations, or visitors from 'topside'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}